--------------------------------
Earlier revisions of ../README.md described this font as "Apache 2.0 / OFL".
That was wrong on the Apache half. The Noto project moved to OFL 1.1 and this
file carries only the OFL notice, quoted above from name ID 13. There is no
Apache-2.0 grant on it.

Derivative works in this tree
-----------------------------
OFL 1.1 §2 requires that the licence and copyright notice accompany any
redistribution of the Font Software, "either as stand-alone or as part of a
larger package", and §1 extends the licence to derivative works. The following
are OFL derivatives of this file and are therefore covered by OFL.txt:

  ../src/fonts/lv_font_noto_thai_14.c
  ../src/fonts/lv_font_noto_thai_16.c
  ../src/fonts/lv_font_noto_thai_20.c
  ../src/fonts/lv_font_noto_thai_24.c
  ../src/fonts/lv_font_noto_thai_28.c

They are produced by ../tools/regen.sh, which runs ../tools/gen_pua_font.py to
build a Private-Use-Area-remapped copy of this font and then rasterises it with
lv_font_conv. The exact command line for each size is recorded in the header
comment of the generated .c file.

Reserved Font Name
------------------
OFL 1.1 §3 forbids using a Reserved Font Name in a Modified Version. The Noto
project does not declare a Reserved Font Name for this family (the OFL header
in OFL.txt carries no "with Reserved Font Name" clause), so the PUA-remapped
intermediate and the rasterised .c fonts may keep the Noto Sans Thai name. Had
a Reserved Font Name been declared, the intermediate NotoSansThai-pua.ttf would
have had to be renamed.

